1903 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Reflection Questions\072\nWhat is the movement concept\077 How should it feel to be the character\077 How would you describe their movement\077\nThe movement is meant to replicate that of Dead Cells\056 In that game\054 the player character feels weighty\054 fast\054 and responsive\056 It should feel like the player is a skilled and agile fighter using a variety of weapons and fighting styles\056\nWhat are some games that you can reference that give you a good sense of this\077\nSeeing as we are trying to directly clone a portion of Dead Cells\054 we should primarily be using that as a reference\056\nWhat do those games to do address Q1\077\nDead cells achieves the things it sets out to by having a relatively strong gravity applied to the character\054 paired with a rather short jump and the ability to cancel almost any animation with a different action\050e\056g\056 rolling mid attack animation\051\056 They also have the character have quite a high base movement speed and the ability to turn on a dime\056\nHow do your settings achieve this goal\077\nI achieved a similar effect as Dead Cells through a couple methods\056 First\054 I borrowed a custom jump function Cate made and dialed in the settings to match what I thought worked best\056 I also turned the gravity scale up on the pawn to around 4\054 and used that to adjust the strength of the jump\056 I adjusted the numbers until jumping from a standstill brought the player up just short of 1 player high\056 This replicates the short\054 weighty jumps in Dead Cells\056 I also adjusted the player\031s movement speed and ground friction to make the movement feel snappier and more responsive\056\nWhat else is needed to make Dead Cells movement\077\nThere are a few missing elements not found in the Unreal Side Scroller pawn\054 such as the ground slam\054 and the dodge roll\056 These are very important to make movement feel correct\054 as they can animation\055cancel out of any other action\054 making the movement feel a lot snappier just by their sheer existence\056 In addition\054 the dodge roll acts almost like a \030dash\031 move\054 which adds a whole other dimension to the movement mechanics\056)
     /K [ 87 ]
     /P 1904 0 R
     /Pg 1816 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1904 0 obj
  << /K [ 86 1903 0 R ]
     /P 1997 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1816 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

