1911 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Why did you choose this example\077 What makes it an effective reference for Moontower\077\nOur plan is to make the game very linear\054 but that doesn\031t mean we can\031t give the player options\056 This example consists of many rooms\057paths of varying elevation\054 that all guide the player towards the same place \050the right side of the screen\051\054 which is a design concept we can apply to Moontower\056 Options within a constrained level\056\n\nWhat player skills does this level test\077 Is it at a beginner\054 intermediate or advanced level of difficulty\077\nThis level tests the player\031s combat skills as well as they\031re ability to platform\056 It also tests the player on how they can combine platforming and combat in a way that benefits their progression through the level\056 \050There were enemies in these empty rooms but they were defeated at the time I took this screenshot\051\056 Given the combination of platforming and combat\054 I would rate this section as intermediate in difficulty\056\n\nDo the aesthetic elements support the overall level design\077 Why or why not\077 \050Include specific examples to back up your argument\051\056\nThe colors used help differentiate the foreground from the background\056 Specifically\054 the use of colder and lighter colors in the background and the use of darker\054 warmer colors in the foreground\056 This creates clarity and removes confusion for the player\056)
     /K [ 95 ]
     /P 1912 0 R
     /Pg 1816 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

