  << /K [ 94 1911 0 R ]
     /P 1997 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1816 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1913 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Why did you choose this example\077 What makes it an effective reference for Moontower\077\nThis example highlights a simple hazardous platforming section\056 It\031s a nice transition section between combat encounters which provides the player more engagement than something like an empty hallway for example\056 Moontower is combat focused\054 so Dead Cells\031 use of a short and simple hazardous platforming section is something we can apply to our game\056\n\nWhat player skills does this level test\077 Is it at a beginner\054 intermediate or advanced level of difficulty\077\nThis tests the player\031s platforming skills at a higher level than the previous example I used\056 Failing a jump in this section is a lot more punishing\054 as the consequences \050loss of health\051 are greater\056 This encourages the player to be much more precise with their inputs\054 and its for this reason that I rate this section as intermediate in difficulty\056\n\nDo the aesthetic elements support the overall level design\077 Why or why not\077 \050Include specific examples to back up your argument\051\056\nSomething to highlight in this example is the way Dead Cells\031 does its environmental hazard\056 The spikes are very distinguishable from the rest of the level elements\056 Their color and shape helps the player see them clearly\054 which is important if you want the player to navigate sections like these effectively\056)
     /K [ 97 ]
     /P 1914 0 R
     /Pg 1816 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

