  << /ActualText (Why did you choose this example\077 What makes it an effective reference for Moontower\077\nI chose this since it is very clearly a \034distinct\035 level segment that breaks up the flow of the game\054 and it stuck with me when playing for that reason\056\nIt would be an effective reference for creating a challenging segment with both dynamic and static hazards\056\nWhat player skills does this level test\077 Is it at a beginner\054 intermediate or advanced level of difficulty\077\nThis segment tests the player\031s ability to time their jumps between the rotating mace hazards\054 but provides a safe area on each platform where the mace will not hit you\056\nIt is an intermediate level of difficulty\056\nDo the aesthetic elements support the overall level design\077 Why or why not\077 \050Include specific examples to back up your argument\051\056\nThe solid elements have a strong level of contrast with the background\054 which immediately helps the player identify where they can platform to\056\nThe hazards all use the same color\054 which helps unify the elements that deal damage\056)
