1939 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Reflection Questions\nWhat is the movement concept\077 How should it feel to be the character\077 How would you describe their movement\077\nThe movement concept is an arcade style platforming character\056 It should feel grounded without being bulky\056 Their movement is fluid and responsive\054 with good in\055air control\056\nWhat are some games that you can reference that give you a good sense of this\077\nDead Cells\054 Skul\072 The Hero Slayer\054 Guacamelee\056\nWhat do those games do to address Q1\077 What do they not do well\077\nDead Cells is the main inspiration\054 and focuses on the flow of the character between combat encounters\056 There are traversal sections\054 but with our character feeling more grounded and human\054 those won\031t translate as well\056\nSkul\072 The Hero Slayer has abilities that drastically change player movement and feel\054 but at it\031s core there is more of a focus on accurate platforming sections\056 These will be helpful to reference for the scale of the world\054 and jump distances for the character\056\nGuacamelee is a good reference for pacing of movement while in a combat encounter\054 especially with multiple enemies in the same room\056 The movement speed and dodge roll are great\054 but jump height and power don\031t work for our concept\056\nHow do your settings achieve this goal\077\nIncreasing gravity scale to 2\0565 gave a more grounded feel without making the character feel heavy or bulky\056\n\034Braking Deceleration Falling\035 controls the lateral deceleration when you are not holding a direction in\055air\054 which acts as a brake\056 I set it to a value of 500\054 this was a good middle ground for accurate control\056 My original value of 1000 acted like a dead stop\054 which felt jarring and out of place for the feel of the game\056\nI increased the rotation rate of the character from 750 to 1080\056 This was a subtle difference\054 yet all of my play\055testers noticed it without prompting\056 This level does not have much need for the player to change direction\054 but it would be more obvious with our currently scoped level design for the game\056\nWHY\056 Just WHY\056\nbc)
     /K [ 123 ]
     /P 1940 0 R
     /Pg 1816 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

