  << /ActualText (Why did you choose this example\077 What makes it an effective reference for Moontower\077\nI chose this example because I found it to be an effective example of how enemy placement and platforming can come together to form an interesting challenge\056 This makes for an effective reference for out project\054 because it is a simple way we can introduce challenge with minimal mechanical cost\056\nWhat player skills does this level test\077 Is it at a beginner\054 intermediate or advanced level of difficulty\077\nThis segment is a beginner segment that tests the player\031s ability to incorporate basic platforming into the combat of the game\056\nDo the aesthetic elements support the overall level design\077 Why or why not\077 \050Include specific examples to back up your argument\051\056\nIn this example\054 there is significant contrast between all elements\054 such as enemies\054 the player\054 solid ground\054 and the background\056 This makes it clear where you as the player are able to stand\054 and where you need to pay attention to avoid getting hurt\056)
