1969 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Why did you choose this example\077 What makes it an effective reference for Moontower\077\nThis example shows another core principle of Dead Cells level design\054 in the multiple ways to approach most enemy encounters\056 I think it makes an effective reference for our game\054 because we want to be cloning it as close as we can\054 and this potential for strategy is an important element of the level design\056\nWhat player skills does this level test\077 Is it at a beginner\054 intermediate or advanced level of difficulty\077\nThis segment is a beginner segment that showcases the potential for approaching combat encounters strategically\054 and tests the player on their ability to do so\056\nDo the aesthetic elements support the overall level design\077 Why or why not\077 \050Include specific examples to back up your argument\051\056\nLike the previous example\054 the contrast between various level elements aid in understanding what\031s going on\054 but this one also adds the interplay between lighting and semi\055solid platforms\054 where light beams shine through the gaps in the platform\054 potentially helping to communicate their semi\055solid nature\056)
     /K [ 153 ]
     /P 1970 0 R
     /Pg 1816 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

