1971 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Why did you choose this example\077 What makes it an effective reference for Moontower\077\nThis final example showcases the exact opposite of the previous one\054 that being the way the level can sometimes provide an intentional bottleneck to force the player to engage with the combat encounter from a specific angle of attack\056 Once again\054 we want to clone Dead Cells as closely as possible\054 but also since out game takes place in a factory\054 it makes sense to have these bottlenecks as the player traverses amidst the machinery and infrastructure\056\nWhat player skills does this level test\077 Is it at a beginner\054 intermediate or advanced level of difficulty\077\nThis segment is a beginner segment that tests the player\031s adaptability in the face of being funneled into an encounter without being able to chose their angle of attack\056\nDo the aesthetic elements support the overall level design\077 Why or why not\077 \050Include specific examples to back up your argument\051\056\nIn addition to the elements discussed in the first example\054 there are now spikes\054 which are also a distinct color palette from everything else\056 This is important\054 because it makes them very evident as a source of danger\056)
     /K [ 155 ]
     /P 1972 0 R
     /Pg 1816 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
